 ## Background
-Training Ray Marching and Integration is based on the volume rendering integral introduced by Mildenhall et al. in 2020 [S3][S5, unofficial]. It has been widely adopted in various NeRF implementations, including instant-ngp [S2, S10, unofficial], jaxngp [S9, unofficial], and others [S1, unofficial][S3][S5, S6, S7, S8, S11, unofficial]. The method has evolved to include optimizations such as occupancy grid pruning [S9, S11, unofficial], hash encoding [S2, S10, unofficial], and adaptive sampling [S2, S10, unofficial].
+Originates from the differentiable volume rendering formulation for NeRF training [S3][S5, unofficial]. It has been widely adopted in various implementations, including instant-ngp [S2, S10, unofficial], jaxngp [S9, unofficial], and others [S1, unofficial][S3][S5, unofficial][S6, unofficial][S7, unofficial][S8, unofficial][S11, unofficial]. The method has evolved to include optimizations such as occupancy grid pruning [S9, unofficial][S11, unofficial], hash encoding [S2, S10, unofficial], and adaptive sampling [S2, S10, unofficial].
 
